  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The meats are no burden to us, most holy father, if the captives ate things which their conquerors set before them, especially since there is one report from all, viz., that the barbarians who have made inroads into our parts have not sacrificed to idols.",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For the apostle says, “Meats for the belly, and the belly for meats: but God shall destroy both it and them.”",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But the Saviour also, who cleanseth all meats, says, “Not that which goeth into a man defileth the man, but that which cometh out.”",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And this meets the case of the captive women defiled by the barbarians, who outraged their bodies.",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But if the previous life of any such person convicted him of going, as it is written, after the eyes of fornicators, the habit of fornication evidently becomes an object of suspicion also in the time of captivity.",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And one ought not readily to have communion with such women in prayers.",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "If any one, however, has lived in the utmost chastity, and has shown in time past a manner of life pure and free from all suspicion, and now falls into wantonness through force of necessity,",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s8",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "we have an example for our guidance,—namely, the instance of the damsel in Deuteronomy, whom a man finds in the field, and forces her and lies with her.",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s9",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "“Unto the damsel,” he says, “ye shall do nothing; there is in the damsel no sin worthy of death:",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s10",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.I.3.s10",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "for as when a man riseth against his neighbour, and slayeth him, even so is this matter: the damsel cried, and there was none to help her.”",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Canon II.",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Covetousness is a great evil; and it is not possible in a single letter to set forth those scriptures in which not robbery alone is declared to be a thing horrible and to be abhorred,",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "but in general the grasping mind, and the disposition to meddle with what belongs to others, in order to satisfy the sordid love of gain.",
    "chunk_index": 14,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And all persons of that spirit are excommunicated from the Church of God. But that at the time of the irruption, in the midst of such woful sorrows and bitter lamentations,",
    "chunk_index": 15,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "some should have been audacious enough to consider the crisis which brought destruction to all the very period for their own private aggrandizement,",
    "chunk_index": 16,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "that is a thing which can be averred only of men who are impious and hated of God, and of unsurpassable iniquity.",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Wherefore it seemed good to excommunicate such persons, lest the wrath (of God) should come upon the whole people, and upon those first of all who are set over them in office, and yet fail to make inquiry.",
    "chunk_index": 18,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For I am afraid, as the Scripture says, lest the impious work the destruction of the righteous along with his own.",
    "chunk_index": 19,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s8",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "“For fornication,” it says, “and covetousness are things on account of which the wrath of God cometh upon the children of disobedience.",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s9",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Be not ye therefore partakers with them. For ye were sometimes darkness, but now are ye light in the Lord:",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s10",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s10",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "walk as children of light (for the fruit of the light is in all goodness, and righteousness, and truth), proving what is acceptable unto the Lord.",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s11",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s11",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And have no fellowship with the unfruitful works of darkness, but rather reprove them; for it is a shame even to speak of those things which are done of them in secret.",
    "chunk_index": 23,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s12",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s12",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But all things that are reproved are made manifest by the light.” In this wise speaks the apostle.",
    "chunk_index": 24,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s13",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s13",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But if certain parties who pay the proper penalty for that former covetousness of theirs, which exhibited itself in the time of peace, now turn aside again to the indulgence of covetousness in the very time of trouble (i.e.,",
    "chunk_index": 25,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s14",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s14",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "in the troubles of the inroads by the barbarians), and make gain out of the blood and ruin of men who have been utterly despoiled, or taken captive,",
    "chunk_index": 26,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle#GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s15",
    "work_id": "anf-works/gregory-thaumaturgus-canonical-epistle",
    "canonical_ref": "GregThaum.EpCan.II.1.s15",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "(or) put to death, what else ought to be expected, than that those who struggle so hotly for covetousness should heap up wrath both for themselves and for the whole people?",
    "chunk_index": 27,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 258,
    "date_range": [
      254,
      262
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
